; tvt_los_hook settings. Read once, when the DLL attaches - change it before
; launching, not during.
;
; mode
;   watch      call the engine's vision function, log what it was asked and
;              what it answered, change nothing. Always safe.
;   deny_far   refuse every sighting beyond deny_beyond metres. Not a model of
;              anything - a crude, unmistakable effect, for proving a decision
;              can be influenced at all.
;   los        the real thing: terrain and foliage occlusion, marched against
;              the mission's own heightfield and zone map.
;
; In every mode this may only ever turn a sighting into a miss. The engine's
; own "not seen" is usually just its detection dice failing on that tick and
; says nothing about geometry, so promoting one would invent information.
;
; In los mode the DLL identifies the loaded mission by itself, by scoring the
; object names in execution.log against every Content.script, and then checks
; that the terrain it loaded actually fits where the units are standing. If
; either step is not decisive it falls back to watch mode and says so in the
; log rather than enforcing against the wrong map.

[los]
mode = los
deny_beyond = 400

; sight_scale, percent. Multiplies every vegetation sight-through distance.
; LOWER makes woods denser and harder to see through. This is the one quantity
; in the model that is calibrated rather than read out of the game's own data,
; so it is meant to be moved.
;
; At 100 a dense conifer stand (zone 11, Forest01) goes opaque at 15 m, so a
; tank 13 m inside one is about 87% masked. At 50 it would be opaque at 7.5 m,
; at 200 at 30 m.
sight_scale = 100

; crew = off | watch
;
; The PLAYER's own gunner is a separate vision system - CAutoShooterComponent,
; not the AI's FUN_100c9e50 - which is why occlusion never changed what you saw
; from the cockpit. "watch" hooks its per-tick update and logs only: it calls
; the original and returns its answer untouched.
;
; This pass exists to confirm the field mapping against a live object before
; anything is denied. Expect RadarMax 3000.0 and ViewAngle 12.0 deg. If those
; two read back correctly we have the right object and can go further.
crew = watch

; gate = off | probe | los
;
; The player gunner's whole target acceptance is one comparison inside its
; update: distance-to-candidate against RadarMaxDistance. "probe" redirects
; only the CALL that computes that distance - five bytes at one address, so no
; other caller of the shared vector-length helper is affected - and logs what
; it sees while returning the true length unchanged.
;
; "los" enforces: the march runs between the two endpoints and a blocked line
; returns a huge length, so the engine's own comparison discards the candidate.
; It can only ever REJECT a target - never make one visible that the engine had
; already dropped.
;
; The endpoints are found by searching the caller's frame for the pair whose
; difference matches the delta, rather than by hardcoded stack offsets. That is
; self-validating: no wrong pair can satisfy the arithmetic.
gate = los

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
; TOTAL BLINDNESS TEST (2026-08-19) - RUN, ANSWERED, mode restored to los
;
; mode=deny_far with deny_beyond=1 refuses EVERY sighting past one metre. Not
; a model of anything - a single unambiguous question:
;
;   AI goes passive, stops shooting  -> FUN_100c9e50 really is the gate, and
;                                       the line-of-sight work is on the right
;                                       lever; whatever is left is tuning.
;   AI fights exactly as normal      -> that function does NOT control
;                                       engagement. Something else does, and
;                                       no amount of occlusion here will ever
;                                       show up in play.
;
; RESULT: 7448 of 7448 positives denied, and every AI unit went silent - so
; FUN_100c9e50 IS the gate for AI units. The player's OWN gunner carried on
; firing normally, because the player's tank never appears as an observer in
; this function at all. Its crew runs on CAutoShooter / CAutoCommander, which
; have their own radar (RadarMaxDistance 3000 / 1500) and a separate path.
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
